.nh
.TH "PB-RECORDINGS-LIST" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-recordings-list - List the recordings you may see


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb recordings list [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
List the recordings you may see

.PP
List a team's terminal recordings you may see: admins see all of them, other members those they may replay. Each row shows the recording ID, machine, start time, length, why it started and whether the machine still holds it.

.PP
Team terminal recordings are made on the recorded machine and stay there, encrypted to the team recording key. Replay is audited by Paperboat before any bytes move, then streams over the end-to-end encrypted machine connection; your unlocked vault opens the key locally.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--all\fP[=false]
	show every item, up to 10000

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for list

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print JSON

.PP
\fB--limit\fP=50
	show at most this many items (1-200)

.PP
\fB--machine\fP=""
	only this machine's recordings (machine id)

.PP
\fB--team\fP=""
	team whose recordings to list; defaults to the active team workspace


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-recordings(1)\fP
